Session end (bugfix round 0.7): the two-layer output pass (its pixel shader and constant buffer, 0017) is made with
each session's device but was not released when the session ended, unlike every other pass of the layer: it kept the
ended session's D3D11 device alive until the next session made new ones (or the process ended).

--- a/openxr-api-layer/layer.cpp
+++ b/openxr-api-layer/layer.cpp
@@ -801,6 +801,10 @@
                     dcsvr::SharedDepthImport().ReleaseAll();
                     m_dcsvrThreeViews.Reset();  // DCSVR three views
                     m_dcsvrThreeViewsLeft.Reset();
+                    // DCSVR two layers: the output pass is made again with the next session's device; kept, it held
+                    // the ended session's device.
+                    m_dcsvrTwoLayerConstants.Reset();
+                    m_dcsvrTwoLayerPS.Reset();
                     dcsvr::SharedDepthImport().SetDevice(nullptr);
                     dcsvr::SharedDepthImport().SetRenderThread(0);
                     m_dcsvrDepthViews.clear();
